ENGLISH
==========================================================================================================

1. What this license covers

   Whitebeard OS (the "Software"): the code in this repository and the packages Whitebeard publishes for it
   (for example, the JARVIS Web package), in any version. Third-party components that the Software downloads
   and installs (Hermes Agent, Paperclip, GBrain, pgvector, Ollama, FFmpeg, Node, uv, Claude Code and
   others) are not part of this license: each one follows its own license.

2. What you may do: personal use

   Whitebeard grants you, as an individual, a free, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to
   download, install, run, copy and modify the Software, on as many of your own machines as you want, for
   personal use only.

   Personal use means use by an individual for their own non-commercial purposes: study, personal
   organization, personal and hobby projects, their home. It is still personal use if you talk to other
   people through the assistants, as long as you receive no payment, direct or indirect, for it.

3. What requires a commercial license

   Any use that is not personal requires a separate, written commercial license from Whitebeard. This
   includes, among others:

   a) use by or on behalf of a company, government body, association or any organization;
   b) use in paid work or to serve clients, including as a freelancer or consultant;
   c) use in the internal operations of a business;
   d) offering the Software, or services based on it, to third parties (hosting, installation, support,
      customization, resale, SaaS);
   e) distributing the Software, modified or not, as part of a product or service.

   For a commercial license: https://whitebeard.dev

4. Sharing

   You may share copies of the Software, modified or not, only for the recipients' personal use, keeping
   this file and the authorship notices. Recipients are bound by this same license.

5. Notices

   Do not remove or change the Software's authorship and license notices.

6. No warranty

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness
   for a particular purpose or freedom from errors. To the extent permitted by law, Whitebeard is not liable
   for damages of any kind arising from the use of the Software, including data loss. You are responsible
   for your backups and for the machines the Software runs on.

7. Termination

   This license ends automatically if you breach it. If you cure the breach within 30 days of being notified
   by Whitebeard, the license is reinstated, once.

8. Governing law

   Brazilian law. Courts of the district where Whitebeard has its registered office.
